<!--
  Novation Launch Control XL 3: a Cadence profile from the online library (A208).

  SOURCE, and only this: the manufacturer's own MIDI documentation.
    Launch Control XL 3 User Guide, Version 2.0 (Focusrite Audio Engineering Ltd (Novation), 2026 (PDF created 2026-01-09)), pages 22 (Using Custom Modes: mode 16 is a fixed default), 23 (Custom Mode settings: Output Port default All), 84 (Settings: Global MIDI Channel default 1), 88 (Appendix: Default Mode (16) parameters)
    https://fael-downloads-prod.focusrite.com/customer/prod/downloads/launch_control_xl_3-pdf-en.pdf
    Launch Control XL 3 programmer's reference guide, Version 1.0 (Focusrite Audio Engineering Ltd (Novation), 2026 (PDF created 2026-04-17)), pages 4 (device ID appended to device name), 5 (MIDI interfaces), 7 (standalone mode), 8-10 (DAW mode, not used here)
    https://fael-downloads-prod.focusrite.com/customer/prod/downloads/launch_control_xl_3_programmer_s_reference_guide-pdf_en.pdf
  No mapping file from any other application was read or used.

  status="manual": the message is the manufacturer's. Nobody has tried this map on the hardware
  yet. If a control does nothing, use Learn on that row and tell us at shlabs.contact@gmail.com.

  BEFORE YOU START: Standalone (MIDI) mode, Custom Mode 16 (the fixed default mode: press Mode, press the 16th mode button, press Mode again). Read from the MIDI In/Out interface (first interface on Windows), not the DAW interface.

  LEFT OUT (no Cadence target): Faders 9-12 (CC9-12): left free.; Button row 2, columns 5-8 (CC49-52): left free.; Page, Track, Record, Play, Shift and Mode buttons: the programmer's reference says "The Page, Track, Record, Play, Solo/Arm and Mute/Select buttons are unused in this mode" (standalone), and Shift/Mode open menus.; DAW mode (enabled by the host with a 9Fh 0Ch 7Fh message): not used, because a profile cannot send that message. In DAW mode the buttons move to channel 1.

  A jog wheel that moves too fast or too slow: set its row to Fine, or invert it, in the dialog.
-->
